@node Overview
@section Overview
The GOAL frontend language is a Lisp-like language for the Eightbol compiler targeting 8-bit and 16-bit retro platforms. This chapter documents the lexical and syntactic features of GOAL, including number literals, identifier normalization, operators, and expressions.

@node Number Formats
@section Number Formats

GOAL supports multiple number literal formats for convenient expression of values across different bases:

@subsection Decimal Literals
Plain sequences of digits represent decimal (base-10) numbers.

@example
42
1000
0
@end example

@subsection Hexadecimal Literals
Hexadecimal numbers are prefixed with @code{#x} and may contain digits 0–9 and letters A–F (case-insensitive).

@example
#xFF
#x1000
#xDEADBEEF
#x0
@end example

@subsection Octal Literals
Octal numbers are prefixed with @code{#o} and may contain digits 0–7.

@example
#o777
#o1000
#o0
@end example

@subsection Binary Literals
Binary numbers are prefixed with @code{#b} and may contain digits 0–1.

@example
#b1111
#b10101010
#b0
@end example

@subsection Dword (String) Literals
Dword or string literals for memory access are prefixed with @code{#d} followed by a quoted string. These are intended for low-level memory operations and platform-specific constant values.

@example
#d"WORD"
#d"DATA"
@end example

@node Identifiers
@section Identifiers

Identifiers in GOAL are sequences of alphanumeric characters, hyphens, underscores, and exclamation marks. The lexer normalizes all identifiers to kebab-case (lowercase with hyphens replacing spaces and underscores) in AST nodes. This normalization ensures consistent representation regardless of input style.

@subsection Identifier Normalization

The front-end converts identifiers to kebab-case form before AST production. This allows flexibility in source code while maintaining consistency in internal representation.

@table @asis
@item @code{PlayerName}
Normalized to @code{player-name}

@item @code{player_score}
Normalized to @code{player-score}

@item @code{PLAYER_HEALTH}
Normalized to @code{player-health}

@item @code{playerId}
Normalized to @code{player-id}
@end table

@node Operators
@section Operators

GOAL supports standard arithmetic, comparison, and bitwise operators:

@table @asis
@item Arithmetic
@code{+} (addition), @code{-} (subtraction), @code{*} (multiplication), @code{/} (division), @code{%} (modulo)

@item Comparison
@code{=} (numeric equal), @code{==} (identity equal), @code{!=} (not equal), @code{<} (less than), @code{>} (greater than), @code{<=} (less than or equal), @code{>=} (greater than or equal)

@item Bitwise
@code{&} (bitwise and), @code{|} (bitwise or), @code{^} (bitwise xor), @code{~} (bitwise not), @code{<<} (left shift), @code{>>} (right shift)

@item Logical
@code{and}, @code{or}, @code{not}

@item Access
@code{.} (member access), @code{->} (pointer dereference)
@end table

@node Expressions
@section Expressions

GOAL supports several forms of expressions:

@subsection S-Expressions (Lists)

S-expressions are enclosed in parentheses and represent function calls or special forms:

@example
(+ 1 2 3)
(defun add (x y) (+ x y))
@end example

@subsection Quoted Expressions

Expressions prefixed with a single quote @code{'} are not evaluated:

@example
'(a b c)
'symbol
@end example

@subsection Conditionals

The @code{if} special form evaluates a test expression and executes one of two branches:

@example
(if (> x 10) (large-operation) (small-operation))
@end example

@node Special Forms
@section Special Forms

GOAL provides the following special forms for control flow and binding:

@table @asis
@item @code{defun}
Defines a named function

@item @code{defmethod}
Defines a method on a class

@item @code{deftype}
Defines a type

@item @code{let}, @code{let*}
Local variable binding

@item @code{if}
Conditional evaluation

@item @code{when}, @code{unless}
One-branch conditionals

@item @code{cond}
Multi-branch conditional

@item @code{case}
Case expression dispatch

@item @code{loop}
Iterative loop

@item @code{quote}
Quote expression (prevent evaluation)

@item @code{lambda}
Anonymous function
@end table
